+Append `md` to a diff command to always receive a Markdown document, including
+for short or empty diffs: `/git diff remote md`, `/git diff md`, or
+`/git diff staged md`. The document includes the comparison base and a fenced
+`diff` block. A partial result is explicitly labelled in the document.
+
+`/git files` lists current tracked and non-ignored untracked files; use
+`/git files src` to narrow it to a directory. `/git file src/example.py` sends
+the current working-tree file as `example.py.md`, with a language-labelled
+code block. No commit or push is needed. Paths are relative to the repository
+root, even when the agent runs from a subdirectory. Type paths containing
+spaces without quotes. Deleted files, ignored untracked files, symlinks,
+binary files, Git metadata and paths outside the repository cannot be viewed.
+Each file is limited to 5 MB; a cut file is labelled as a partial view.
+Existing secret-redaction settings also apply to these documents.
